               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 11/08/2026 with an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed to assess respiratory status and exclude pneumonia or pneumothorax. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. He was treated with inhaled bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy with good clinical response. He was discharged on 12/08/2026 in a stable condition. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me if you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
